<title>SWITZERLAND: SNB LEAVES DISCOUNT RATE AT ONE PCT AFTER MEETING.</title>
<headline>SNB LEAVES DISCOUNT RATE AT ONE PCT AFTER MEETING.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss National Bank (SNB) said it was leaving its discount rate unchanged at one percent after a regular weekly meeting of its board.</p>
<p>The rate has been held at one percent since it was lowered by half a percentage point to the current level on September 26, 1996.</p>
<p>At the current level the rate matches the historic low maintained from February 1978 to November 1979.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
